---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
---

<Base title="About" description={`About ${SITE.author}.`}>
  <article class="prose-wrap">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Hi, I’m Ram.</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Yes, it’s hidden in the name: pa<strong>ram</strong>. A parameter is the one value you change to see how a
        system behaves, and that’s the whole idea behind this lab.
      </p>
      <p>
        I’m an engineer who learns best by building. This site is where I do that in public: every project is
        open source, every episode ships working code, and every explanation is something you can run and change.
      </p>
      <p>
        I build with AI as a pair programmer, mostly Claude Code, and I’m open about it. The point isn’t to look clever.
        It’s to show how learning and building actually work now, mistakes included.
      </p>
      <h2>Why this exists</h2>
      <p>
        Most of what I learned stuck because I broke something and had to understand why. Reading about a bug teaches
        less than causing it yourself. So everything here is built so you can cause it yourself, safely, in your browser.
      </p>
      <h2>Find me</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href={SITE.github}>GitHub</a></li>
        <li><a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  header { padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 4.5rem) 0.5rem; }
</style>
